# rcmain: what rc runs before its first command. In the image now, on the
# disk later. Every default yields to what /env already held.
if(~ $#path 0) path=(. /bin)
if(~ $#home 0) home=/usr/glenda
if(~ $#ifs 0) ifs=(' ' '	' '
')
if(~ $#prompt 0) prompt=('% ' '	')

# 9fs: mount another machine's tree at /n/host, the two lines as one.
# `srv` dials tcp!host!9fs and posts the stream; `mount` makes it a tree.
fn 9fs { srv tcp!$1!9fs $1 && mount /srv/$1 /n/$1 }

# login: become a person for the rest of this session. `exec` so `auth`
# replaces this shell rather than a child of it -- the passphrase, the
# name into the kernel and /env, and a fresh shell all land on the one
# process that owns the console. docs/FLEET.md section 4.
fn login { exec auth login $1 }
